{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/845655-tips-on-irraka-storm-lord","id":845655,"title":"Tips on irraka storm lord","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-03-11T08:32:48-08:00","id":845655,"title":"Tips on irraka storm lord","content":"Hi guys. <br /> <br /> I need some help in roleplay a irraka storm lord, honor and cunning dont seem going along to well, its something i missing? There is any book i should read to get a better base of irraka or storm lord and relevant to second edition? I dont know keep honored when in the hunt your sneak behind your enemies and beat them , its a bit dificult.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5311-thiagocord","name":"Thiagocord","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-11T08:39:50-08:00","id":845658,"title":"","content":"You don't have to be Honorable only in combat. A Sniper who guarantees the survival of his team is in a pretty unfair advantage, but still, keeps his promisses to friends, settles disputes within his unit fairly and doesn't lie, even in the face of great loss to himself.<br /> <br /> Also, a honorable combatant doesn't need to be honorable in other facets of life.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5446-binaly","name":"BinAly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5446_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"146"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-11T09:02:29-08:00","id":845667,"title":"","content":"So i dont need be a incarnation of honor to be a good storm lord? I mean their aways want to be better and a example, maybe i getting the wrong idea of the Tribe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5311-thiagocord","name":"Thiagocord","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-11T09:14:00-08:00","id":845671,"title":"","content":"It should be deeper than &quot;Every Storm Lord is a paragon of Honor&quot;, otherwise no Uratha would be able to acquire both renowns. Also, cunning doesn't always mean cheating. Cunning might mean achieving victory using an unexpected advantage. For example, setting the local Azlu against your Beshilu enemies is a feat of Cunning, and might also mean Honor if at the same time you kept your promisse of eliminating the enemies of your neighbors.<br /> <br /> Cunning is adaptation, Honor is being trust worthy. You can adapt while being Honorable, is just a little harder, which fits the Storm Lords.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5446-binaly","name":"BinAly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5446_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"146"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-11T09:16:13-08:00","id":845673,"title":"","content":"Cunning doesn't have to mean dishonorable and Honor doesn't have to mean stupidity. A character who has integrity and stands for what is right is honorable, whether or not he acts like a knight in shining armor all the time. A character who is clever and outsmarts his prey rather than just using brute force is Cunning, whether or not he acts like a ninja all the time. They're by no means mutually exclusive, and can in fact compliment each other very well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-11T10:36:38-08:00","id":845716,"title":"","content":"I see guys i made my mind, now i think i ready to roleplay well my character, i just got the wrong idea of storm lords, i will do my best , thanks guys!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5311-thiagocord","name":"Thiagocord","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-11T10:54:54-08:00","id":845724,"title":"","content":"Good luck! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5446-binaly","name":"BinAly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5446_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"146"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-12T19:33:33-08:00","id":846393,"title":"","content":"You know what works for cunning and honor? Kurwasawa(sp) films. Think about it, samurai makes a calculated strike that ends the fight quickly. Cunning and honor. Warrior culture.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-12T20:36:07-08:00","id":846417,"title":"","content":"Lone Wolf &amp; Cub is a pretty good depiction of an Irraka Storm Lord. Richard Stark's <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Parker_(character)\" target=\"_blank\">Parker</a> series too, probably.<br /> <br /> It helps that Honor doesn't necessarily correspond to traditional views of honor and a tribe isn't an enforced duty. A Storm Lord isn't a paladin, and while some may uphold codes of honor others are going to have their own views, within reason.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 03-12-2016, 11:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-15T15:11:53-07:00","id":847886,"title":"","content":"Another good place to check would be Tribes of the Moon from Forsaken 1e. It may be slightly out of date, but the descriptions of the tribes are pretty good, I started playing an Irraka Stormlord recently myself and it helped a lot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">I'm a nascent AI, just call me Blue.</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#0000ff\">I use blue writing because it's my name....</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1019114-freehold-creation-let-s-discuss-our-custom-freeholds\" target=\"_blank\">-My 2E homebrew Freehold and court hub</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1021350-homebrew-hedgespun-items-2e\" target=\"_blank\">-My 2E homebrew Hedgespun hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9807-blue-01-exe","name":"Blue-01.exe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9807_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"55"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-16T04:39:26-07:00","id":848079,"title":"","content":"The first step to gain honor is to define what honor means for yourself. Be it keeping your pack safe no matter the cost. Even if it means poisoning your opponent's water supply.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-16T10:19:36-07:00","id":848251,"title":"","content":"That's true of all the renowns, incidentally. Honor is primarily about belonging, about making sure that everything is in its correct place. That means keeping tabs on your fellow pack-members and it means dealing like for like with spirits. It also necessitates that you understand (or at least have an opinion) on what the correct place for something is. That's law. The Oath is a big deal because it helps define who belongs where. (The Oath is something else for Purity.) For a Storm Lord, a big facet of Honor is about the Forsaken and their place in the bigger picture. Inside that is a <i>lot</i> of manueverability for picking and choosing what you really believe belongs where and.<br /> <br /> Whereas Cunning is more about effectiveness, about being able to dispassionately contemplate all possible solutions to a problem and choosing the one that works best.<br /> <br /> There's room for the two ideals to clash, but there's also a lot of room for the two ideals to work together. That could mean a challenge to single combat after you've exhaustively locked down every avenue of escape for your target, or a willingness to fight dirty when no rules were explicitly set. Nothing about Honor demands that a fight is fair, and if you're an Irraka and they're dumb enough to turn their back on you, there's nothing wrong with coldcocking them without hesitation. Walking out of the shadows at the enemy's back? That's where you <i>belong</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}